From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 13:10:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: reset the module by GPIO at a firmware reload

A full chip reset and a power-on after idle power-off reset only the
WiFi subsystem before they load firmware again. Some modules then
answer init commands, but their first channel set times out, and a
full reset repeats without end.

Each firmware reload first resets the module through the reset GPIO
of its PCIe controller; without it, a reload keeps the WFSYS reset
only. The driver looks up that reset at run time, because the module
must also load on a kernel without it. The driver stores config space
of both PCI functions at probe, because a function that does not
answer has no config to save. While a link is down, the driver fences
register access, keeps TX in reset and refuses MCU commands, and the
core skips its ring accesses. After the last failed try, the driver
marks the chip off, so that the next start resets the module and
starts its radios again. A chip that refuses driver own at power-on
gets a module reset, because register reads work after that reset.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
